dow on the church on Royal in the Quarter). This is a great addition to the community and I look forward to more events here. I took one star off because the building is rather cold in co..."},{"business_id":"kPSbSxcnp3kqxGYhHfoDww","review_id":"ldCohS3Fv2B5XMp9xp_FIQ","date":"2014-03-23T03:39:02","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9250604510307312,"text_excerpt":"I had a chance to visit this location for Nola Fashion Week. I definitely see the potential in this beautiful building that was once a Trinity Church in the Bywater. Even as it is in repair stage it has character and beautiful. It was a ideal venue for a fashion show, especially with the long walk way. This space is right in the midst of a residential community so parking can definitely be limited if ever attending an event in this location."},{"business_id":"kPSbSxcnp3kqxGYhHfoDww","review_id":"8HhZrr7oEPHuLvbHdemB5g","date":"2013-11-18T14:03:15","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.918907880783081,"text_excerpt":"I stopped by here for a meeting, and had never really been in the space before. I didn't spend much time there so this review is going to be somewhat incomplete, but the building is incredible. An old church sanctuary, it has a very interesting interior. I think the space hosts a lot of art shows and performances. I'm not sure if you'd really seek out this space unless there was an event going on, but it's quite memorable once you step inside."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
